course: dictionary
lesson: 9870
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one is right. The word tab is a good example. «Lateral reading means checking a website by opening a new tab and reading what others say about it.» Here you open a tab in a web browser, so a tab is one of the pages open on the screen.
explain: The same word can be used in other ways. «RAM is fast working memory, like a desk; every open program or browser tab takes some of it.» Each open tab uses a little of the computer's memory, so tab is still a browser page here.
explain: Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence. A tab can also be a small flap for pulling, as on a drink can, or a bill you pay later. Try each meaning in the sentence and see which one makes sense.
fact: A tab is a small flap or strip sticking out of something, used for pulling, holding or labelling it, like the tab on a can.
fact: On a computer, a tab is one of the pages open in a web browser, shown as a little label along the top.
fact: The Tab key on a keyboard moves the cursor forward to the next space or box.
fact: «Put it on my tab» is informal and means put the bill for food or drink on my account and pay later.
fact: «Keep tabs on» someone means to watch them carefully to know what they are doing.
exercise: In «Lateral reading means checking a website by opening a new tab», what is a tab? | A bill for food | A strip of cloth on a shirt | *A page open in a web browser | A flap sticking out of a can
exercise: What does the Tab key on a keyboard do? | Turns the computer off | Locks the screen | Prints the page | *Moves the cursor to the next space or box
exercise: Mia says, «Put it on my tab.» What does she mean? | Throw the drink away | Give the drink to a friend for free | Stick a label on the can | *Put the bill on my account and I will pay later
test: In «every open program or browser tab takes some of it», what does tab mean? | *One of the open pages in a browser | A bill for food | A flap on a can | A way to pull a drawer open
test: Dad says, «Keep tabs on the children at the park.» What does keep tabs on mean? | *Watch them carefully | Forget about them | Give them a drink | Buy them lunch
exam: Which meaning fits «Pull the tab on the can to open the drink»? | *A small flap or strip for pulling | A bill for food | A page open in a web browser | A label on a web page
